  "readmeFile": "README.md",
  "releaseNotes": "1.2.4 adds GenerateDualLinkAsync (links-only): from a single productId/URL it returns just the TWO affiliate links (site + app) in a SINGLE batched link.generate call, skipping productdetail.get entirely. This is the preferred path when the caller already has product data (title/price/image) from another source such as a cross-tenant cache — only the per-tenant links are missing, and the productdetail call (the one that most often hits ApiCallLimit, dropping the photo) is avoided. 1.2.4 also spaces the two calls in GenerateDualLinkWithDetailsAsync: a configurable pause (AliExpressAffiliateOptions.DelayBetweenLinkAndDetailMilliseconds, default 1000ms; 0 disables) is inserted between link.generate and productdetail.get, giving the ~1 req/s app quota room to recover BEFORE the rate-limited call instead of only retrying after it fails. 1.2.3 adds GenerateDualLinkWithDetailsAsync: from a single productId/URL it returns BOTH affiliate links (site + app) of the same product plus product details (title/price/image) using only 2 AliExpress calls — one batched link.generate (source_values=site,app) and one productdetail.get with built-in backoff retry on ApiCallLimit. This replaces the previous dual-link flow that made ~4 calls (link.generate + productdetail per variant) and silently dropped the rate-limited productdetail, publishing offers without a photo. 1.2.2 makes product-detail enrichment best-effort during affiliate link generation: when GenerateAffiliateLinkAsync(IncludeProductDetails=true) succeeds on the link.generate call but the follow-up productdetail.get call fails (e.g. ApiCallLimit rate limiting, internal timeout, or non-catalog product), the already-generated affiliate link is now returned WITHOUT product details instead of throwing and discarding the link. Caller cancellation still propagates. 1.2.1 was a maintenance release (CI workflow + package metadata, no API changes). 1.2.0 adds AliExpressAffiliateCredentialException and AliExpressAffiliateCredentialFailureKind so callers can distinguish rejected AliExpress Open Platform credentials from transient HTTP failures and non-affiliable products. HTTP 401/403 and Open Platform signature/app key/session/permission errors now surface as non-retryable credential failures.",
